{"name":"Fragrant Coriander","hex":"#eabc83","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fragrant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sweet-smelling; having a pleasant (usually strong) scent or fragrance.","Attractive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fragrant"},{"term":"coriander","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The annual herb Coriandrum sativum, used in many cuisines.","The dried fruits thereof, used as a spice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coriander"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coriander","blocks":[{"text":"Coriander, or Coriandrum sativum, is an annual herb in the family Apiaceae. The leaves are known as cilantro in the US. Most people perceive the leaves as having a fresh, slightly citrus taste. Due to variations in the gene OR6A2, some people perceive its flavor to be more soaplike or rotten."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Coriandrum_sativum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-193.jpg/330px-Coriandrum_sativum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-193.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coriander","wikidata":"Q41611"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Coriandrum_sativum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-193.jpg/330px-Coriandrum_sativum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-193.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Coriandrum_sativum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-193.jpg/330px-Coriandrum_sativum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-193.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoriandrum_sativum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-193.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/com